 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Capability matrix (part 3/3)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Capability matrix": · Automation · recurring workflows and monitoring · Automations · trigger, action graph, guardrails, observability · 
 · 3D / Media · multimodal creation and transformation · Create / More · artifact contract, renderer/engine evidence · 
 · Trust · truth, evidence, confidence and conflicts · contextual · evidence, provenance, temporal truth, decision · 
 · Safety · privacy, permissions, confirmations and governance · Settings · policy decision, authorization, audit ·','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','7d8d53a7572b8a1f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Universal execution contract','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Universal execution contract": Every substantive request follows the same conceptual path:
goal → intent → context → evidence → plan → skill composition → tool/agent execution → verification → truth decision → authorized action → result → memory update → explanation
Not every request needs every stage visibly. The runtime may short-circuit simple requests while preserving the same contracts.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','19d8ebe45d4b7e94'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — One model, many modes','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "One model, many modes": fresh-unified-1 supports capability modes such as:
- Fast — low-latency everyday assistance.
- Think — deeper reasoning and structured analysis.
- Deep Think — complex planning and verification.
- Research — evidence-first investigation.
- Create — multimodal generation and transformation.
- Work — long-running, permissioned execution.
Modes are routing/runtime policies over the same Fresh model identity. They must not silently create provider-specific model identities.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','d505398a918ee06b'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Memory contract','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Memory contract": Fresh AI may maintain distinct memory classes under one memory fabric:
- conversation
- personal
- preference
- project
- task/working
- semantic knowledge
- episodic/event
- media/context
- skill/learning
- temporal/provenance
Memory writes require an explicit policy decision. Sensitive or durable memory must be user-controlled, traceable and correctable. Forgetting must remove the relevant durable representation according to the platform retention contract rather than merely hiding it from the UI.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','21afbb644d703eb0'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Tool and agent contract','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Tool and agent contract": Tools are capability executors. Agents are operational managers. Neither is a second intelligence identity.
Every tool/action declares:
capability → inputs → required permissions → risk class → execution boundary → evidence/result → verification → rollback/compensation
Sensitive actions require approval before execution. Financial, destructive, identity, publication and security-sensitive operations remain behind explicit safety boundaries.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','8c83be15f1271da9'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Artifact contract','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Artifact contract": Fresh AI can create or transform:
- text and documents
- spreadsheets and datasets
- presentations
- code and project files
- images and avatars
- audio
- video
- 3D assets/scenes
- research reports
- diagrams and structured knowledge
Every persistent artifact needs an owner, provenance, capability version and storage/reference boundary. A generated artifact must never be represented as successfully generated if its required engine was unavailable.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','02fd9a31c7107b41'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Truth and explanation contract','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Truth and explanation contract": For material claims, Fresh AI preserves the states:
KNOWN · SUPPORTED · PROBABLE · UNCERTAIN · CONTRADICTED · UNKNOWN · BLOCKED
Explanations expose conclusions, evidence, uncertainty, decisions and action status. They do not expose private chain-of-thought or proprietary implementation details.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','d9beb154fbb1e595'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Evaluation gate','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Evaluation gate": A capability is not considered production-complete merely because a button exists. Each capability requires:
1. typed contract;
2. real implementation boundary;
3. permission boundary;
4. unit tests;
5. integration tests;
6. end-to-end coverage where user-visible;
7. adversarial/safety tests where applicable;
8. regression cases;
9. observability and failure reporting;
10. truthful degraded behavior when dependencies are unavailable.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','920a5bf25f33df9d'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Training gate','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Training gate": Training may expand the intelligence of fresh-unified-1, but training must not be used to define missing product contracts. The capability surface, tool boundaries, memory model, truth system, permissions and evaluation harness must exist first.
The current repository explicitly marks the Fresh checkpoint as training-required; this contract does not claim that trained foundation-model weights already exist.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','11fd01df930af954'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT — Non-negotiables','Per docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md (Fresh AI Capability & Product Contract (#TRUEMODE)), section "Non-negotiables": - No hidden provider API dependency in Fresh AI core.
- No fake buttons that imply unsupported execution.
- No fabricated search, computation, generation or action results.
- No duplicate reasoning/memory systems inside individual agents.
- No destructive action without authorization.
- No silent deletion of conflicting evidence.
- No exposing secrets, private architecture or chain-of-thought to end users.
- Preserve existing working product behavior while migrating to canonical contracts.','docs/FRESH_AI_CAPABILITY_PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md','dedf37334e50ce26'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_COMPLETION — What “done” means here','Per docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md (Fresh AI completion status — capability-specific readiness), section "What “done” means here": Fresh AI must not be summarized with a single completion percentage. Architecture files and static contract checks establish that boundaries exist; they do not prove every capability is live, production-ready, or verified in the deployed browser. Use the capability registry and runtime checks to determine readiness.
 · Layer · Status · 
 · Application (UI, API, vault, gateway, governance, doctrine) · Partially wired; production readiness not established · 
 · Foundation weights (fresh-unified-1) · training-required · 
 · Server-blind live E2EE · blocked until on-device inference ·','docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md','a245d8b9394d3e5a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_COMPLETION — End-to-end encrypted (at rest)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md (Fresh AI completion status — capability-specific readiness), section "End-to-end encrypted (at rest)": 1. Unlock vault (passphrase ≥8 chars, or ephemeral session key).
2. Send messages as usual (server still sees plaintext for inference).
3. After each answer, client seals latest user+assistant turns → POST /api/ai/conversations seal-latest.
4. On reload, unlock with same passphrase (salt/kid stored in localStorage) to decrypt history.
Not end-to-end for the live request path: /api/ai/ask must read the goal until a local checkpoint exists.','docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md','1d0b44e67bcd02d6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_COMPLETION — Reproduce vault','Per docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md (Fresh AI completion status — capability-specific readiness), section "Reproduce vault": - Crypto: src/core/crypto/FreshE2EE.ts, FreshSecureVault.ts
- UI: vault bar in FreshAIUnified
- API: api/ai/conversations.ts POST seal-latest
- Test: npm run test:fresh-e2ee','docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md','429497cb30952303'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_COMPLETION — Remaining 1%+','Per docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md (Fresh AI completion status — capability-specific readiness), section "Remaining 1%+": 1. Full-capacity GPU training + eval + promotion → change weightsStatus
2. Optional on-device inference path for true request-path E2EE
3. Deeper TRUEMODE labels on every answer in UI','docs/FRESH_AI_COMPLETION.md','15385c169e08a93a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP — Fresh AI independence roadmap','Per docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI independence roadmap), section "Fresh AI independence roadmap": Principle: no outside AI model at runtime. Not Gemini, DeepSeek, OpenAI, Claude or any other.
Fresh AI reasons, remembers, retrieves, verifies and creates with Fresh-owned code and data.','docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md','ca90974bf02f079a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP — What is already independent (verified in code)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI independence roadmap), section "What is already independent (verified in code)": - Goal understanding (FreshGoalUnderstanding), kernel, reasoning and verification layers.
- 11 native dimensional engines (FreshNativeDimensionalEngines) and the native generation
 fabric, both asserted network-free and provider-independent by CI.
- Truth states, TRUEMODE gating, per-user memory, per-user sealed conversations.
- Knowledge: freshaiknowledge (74 rows live: 16 hand-written + 58 generated from the
 master matrix) and freshaitraining_examples (138 live).
- fresh-unified-1 is declared providerIndependent: true, externalProviderRequired: false,
 weightsStatus: "training-required". That last field is the honest status.','docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md','ec573190f93ee54d'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP — What the v3 bundle changes','Per docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI independence roadmap), section "What the v3 bundle changes": - Removes the Gemini interpret/answer code from api/ai/ask.ts. The endpoint can no longer
 send any text to an outside model, even if an environment variable is set by mistake.
- Grounds answers in Fresh''s own knowledge on every request.
- Keeps FRESHALLOWEXTERNALANSWERPROVIDER unset. CI still requires that opt-in string
 in the gateway, so leave the gateway guard in place and never set the variable.','docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md','1b3c2a09c9c64e99'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP — Remaining non-AI dependencies (decide per item)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI independence roadmap), section "Remaining non-AI dependencies (decide per item)": facts, or replace later with a Fresh crawler and index.
- Supabase, Vercel, GitHub: infrastructure.
- Inert placeholder connectors for openai, anthropic, google-gemini and meta-ai are
 registered in src/features/ai/intelligence/registerConnectors.ts. They make no calls.
 Remove them if you do not want those names shown in the UI.','docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md','947ea6ff8760ba99'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP — Stages','Per docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI independence roadmap), section "Stages": 1. Knowledge-first assistant (this bundle). Accurate and honest, but not conversational.
2. Better retrieval with no outside AI: Postgres full-text search (tsvector + GIN index +
 websearchtotsquery ranking) on freshaiknowledge. Then ingest every doc in docs/
 with a generator like scripts/generate-fresh-knowledge-from-matrix.mjs.
3. Learning loop: thumbs up/down in freshaifeedback creates candidate knowledge and
 preference pairs; the owner approves them (AI Governance already requires approval).
4. Train fresh-unified-1: needs a large first-party or consented corpus with provenance,
 a tokenizer, and GPU time. A small model trained on Fresh data can answer Fresh questions
 fluently. General open-ended conversation at the level of major assistants needs billions
 of tokens and very large compute, which is not realistic soon. Plan for domain-level
 independence first.','docs/FRESH_AI_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md','20e3dd074f172644'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_LEARNING_LOOP — Fresh AI learning loop (no outside AI)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_LEARNING_LOOP.md (Fresh AI learning loop (no outside AI)), section "Fresh AI learning loop (no outside AI)": 1. A user presses the thumbs-down on an answer. Fresh AI asks what it should have said.
2. If the user types a correction and then explicitly confirms sharing, the question, the
 answer and the correction are stored in freshaipreferencepairs with
 safetychecked = false. Nothing is shared without that confirmation.
3. The owner reviews corrections in the Supabase SQL editor:
4. Approve a good one. This adds it to Fresh AI knowledge, searchable immediately:
5. Reject a bad one:
Approved corrections are also high-quality training pairs for fresh-unified-1. Only rows with
safety_checked = true should ever be used for training.','docs/FRESH_AI_LEARNING_LOOP.md','c3c7cd55d4b7ba2c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Fresh AI Readiness Audit','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Fresh AI Readiness Audit": Purpose: keep Fresh AI''s UI, runtime capabilities, and model training status separate. A route, button, registry entry, or passing static contract test is not proof that a capability is production-ready.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','d5616401ded75c2e'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Implemented code foundations — end-to-end production verification still required (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Implemented code foundations — end-to-end production verification still required": - One entry surface: FreshAIUnified is the canonical UI for /ai; the global entry is on-demand and dismissible.
- Request boundaries: /api/ai/ask and /api/ai/stream route requests through the Fresh AI intelligence gateway.
- Context and orchestration: the gateway assembles workspace context, intent, evidence, capability resolutions, planning, verification, and governance decisions.
- Conversation persistence boundary: conversation APIs and a ledger path exist; live persistence depends on valid server configuration and must be smoke-tested.
- Files and media boundaries: authenticated file upload and Fresh-owned media persistence/image-generation contracts exist; each engine must be tested with its required configuration.
- Native dimensional engines: 1D–11D engine contracts are registered. Their presence does not mean the trained foundation model supports every modality.
- Governance and truth: approval checks and fail-closed execution boundaries exist; real tool execution, audit coverage, and rollback/compensation need capability-by-capability verification.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','e21f1b49f8c6ffc6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Implemented code foundations — end-to-end production verification still required (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Implemented code foundations — end-to-end production verification still required": - Vault: client-side sealing for stored conversation turns exists. This is encryption at rest, not server-blind live inference.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','91e875b4e944fd88'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Capability readiness (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Capability readiness": The registry''s implemented status means a Fresh-owned code boundary is present. It is not a blanket statement that production dependencies are configured or the deployed end-to-end flow has passed.
 · Capability group · Registry status · Current treatment · 
 · Conversation · Implemented · Available through the unified composer; production smoke test still required · 
 · Search and Research · Implemented · Keep available, but verify configured retrieval, current sources, provenance, and truthful degraded behavior · 
 · Create · Implemented · Available only through supported generation boundaries; report engine/configuration failures clearly · 
 · Files · Implemented · Authenticated upload boundary exists; vision/camera understanding is not implied · 
 · Memory, Trust, Safety · Implemented · Verify persistence, evidence, approval, and audit behavior end to end · 
 · Voice, Vision/Camera · Contracted · Not yet a complete executable capability · 
 · Data, Code, Projects, Knowledge, Skills · Contracted · Show as in development, not as working execution controls ·','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','9e26c432c65536d4'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Capability readiness (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Capability readiness": · Apps, Work, Tasks, Library, Automations · Contracted · Require real connector/tool boundaries, permissions, audit, and verification · 
 · 3D / broader media · Contracted · Native dimensional contracts do not establish complete media-generation readiness · 
The unified UI must read these states from the canonical capability registry. Contracted capabilities should be visibly marked In development and disabled until a real runtime boundary is available.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','f491f402747ce467'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Optional image inference adapter — implemented contract, deployment configuration required (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Optional image inference adapter — implemented contract, deployment configuration required": Fresh AI now has a Fresh-owned adapter boundary for a separately deployed image inference engine. The adapter is opt-in and uses the same authenticated Fresh request path, Fresh model identity, artifact persistence, and provenance contract.
Server-only Vercel environment variables:
The engine accepts JSON with contract, modelId, kind, prompt, size, and quality; it returns { "b64Json": "<base64 PNG>", "mimeType": "image/png" }. The URL and token are never accepted from the browser, and the configured inference path requires a signed-in user. Remote HTTPS, redirect rejection, a 45-second timeout, payload bounds, PNG signature validation, and persisted engine provenance are enforced by the Fresh server boundary.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','b804536d50d5ecb9'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Optional image inference adapter — implemented contract, deployment configuration required (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Optional image inference adapter — implemented contract, deployment configuration required": If the engine URL is not configured, Fresh AI tries its native generation runtime. That runtime currently truthfully reports training-required until actual Fresh-trained image weights and an inference backend are registered and verified. Configuring the adapter makes a real external inference engine available to Fresh AI; it does not mean such an engine is already deployed or that image generation has passed production smoke tests.
Regression contract: npm run test:fresh-ai-image-engine. This static contract test is not a substitute for a configured-engine integration test, authenticated image-generation test, storage test, or deployed production smoke test.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','ea7f934ee2d867c1'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Model training: current facts','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Model training: current facts": - Model identity: fresh-unified-1.
- The starter run fresh-unified-1-starter-run1 completed 40 CPU optimizer steps on 46 synthetic authorized examples.
- The starter architecture was deliberately reduced for a pipeline smoke test: hidden size 128, 2 layers, feed-forward size 256, context 256.
- The reported final loss was approximately 107.75. This is not evidence of useful production intelligence.
- The repository still declares weightsStatus: training-required.
- Run 3 (fresh-unified-1-run3, 2026-10-29): a 49.9M-parameter model trained from scratch on 32.3M authorized, screened tokens reached held-out perplexity 42.0 (run 2 with a bad initialization: 356). Output is fluent-looking but not reliably correct; no safety, truthfulness or capability evaluation has run. See docs/FRESHAITRAINING_RUN3.md. Still training-required.
- inferFreshUnified currently returns training-required; even a registered checkpoint is not served because the native neural backend is not installed.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','bcac16979e4ed7f4'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Gates before model promotion','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Gates before model promotion": 1. Prepare a substantially larger, lawful, provenance-tracked corpus with verified training and derivative-model permissions.
2. Train the versioned Fresh tokenizer on authorized data and record its hash.
3. Run full-spec foundation training with suitable GPU compute; the v1 target is vocabulary 32,000, context 2,048, hidden size 512, 8 transformer layers, 8 attention heads, and feed-forward size 2,048.
4. Complete held-out capability evaluations, truth/grounding tests, safety review, robustness and regression evaluation.
5. Install and verify the native serving backend; register and hash the actual checkpoint and manifest.
6. Promote only after provenance, integrity, evaluation, and serving gates pass. Do not set the model to ready merely because training completed.
7. Train multimodal encoders/decoders and action heads as later stages; text training alone does not complete vision, audio, video, 3D, or tool-use intelligence.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','e25dcf0edfbf7fbd'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Privacy boundary','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Privacy boundary": The vault can seal stored turns, but the live /api/ai/ask inference path currently receives plaintext. Server-blind live end-to-end encryption remains blocked until an on-device inference path is implemented and verified. The UI and documentation must not imply otherwise.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','104fc16abfdba919'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Engineering sequence (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Engineering sequence": 1. Unify the surface and remove persistent UI takeover. Route /ai through the canonical component, keep the global entry on-demand, and prevent unsupported modes from appearing executable.
2. Prove the core request loop. Test chat, cancellation, errors, session restore, conversation persistence, and context preservation with configured dependencies. Use existing no-cost CI and local/preview testing; do not create a paid staging resource.
3. Complete Research + Trust. Verify source retrieval, citations, provenance, uncertainty, contradictions, and honest no-source behavior.
4. Complete Files + Vision. Test upload, access control, document parsing, image understanding, and camera entry points separately.
5. Complete Create. Test image generation and persistence first, then audio/video/3D only where real engines exist.
6. Complete governed work. Connect executable tools only with explicit permissions, approvals, audit events, verification, and rollback/compensation.
7. Train and serve the model. Follow the training gates above; don''t use training to conceal missing product contracts.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','b37245e6b9394793'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Engineering sequence (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Engineering sequence": 8. Verify the deployed product. Run mobile/accessibility checks, production smoke tests, and capability-specific regressions before marking any capability done.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','1b9c566069061ac2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT — Definition of done','Per docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md (Fresh AI Readiness Audit), section "Definition of done": A capability is complete only when its implementation, permissions, configured dependencies, end-to-end test, observability, verification, and truthful failure behavior are demonstrated. The overall product has no single trustworthy completion percentage.','docs/FRESH_AI_READINESS_AUDIT.md','a1009ea162f29169'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Canonical product contract','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Canonical product contract": Fresh AI is one sovereign model identity, fresh-unified-1, with a canonical capability registry and product contract. The product contract is defined in docs/FRESHAICAPABILITYPRODUCTCONTRACT.md and the runtime registry in src/core/fresh-ai/FreshAICapabilityRegistry.ts.
The runtime must grow capabilities without turning them into separate provider-shaped brains.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','d1d46077a7be76ec'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Current foundation','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Current foundation": 1. Canonical backend — /api/ai/ask remains the primary Fresh AI request boundary.
2. Unified UI — FreshAIUnified is the application-level Fresh AI surface.
3. Sovereign model boundary — fresh-unified-1 is provider-independent and explicitly does not require an external AI provider for its core contract.
4. Native generation boundary — image/avatar creation is routed through Fresh-owned generation contracts; the repository does not claim trained foundation-model weights where they do not exist.
5. Persistence — Fresh AI state/events use the existing Supabase-backed persistence boundaries.
6. Verification — Fresh AI has integrity checks for the unified model, native generation and capability contracts.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','ead2f8f41dc2b422'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Product surface to implement progressively','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Product surface to implement progressively": Primary entry points:
Ask Fresh · Voice · Search · Create · Research · Work · Files · Camera
Secondary capabilities:
Code · Data · Projects · Tasks · Knowledge · Library · Skills · Apps · Automations · 3D · Video · Settings
These are capability entry points, not permission to display fake controls. A control becomes user-visible only when its implementation boundary and truthful degraded state are ready.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','495365df49af30b0'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Runtime layers','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Runtime layers": 1. Intent and context assembly.
2. Memory and knowledge retrieval.
3. Evidence and truth decision.
4. Skill discovery and composition.
5. Plan generation and checkpoints.
6. Tool and agent execution behind permissions.
7. Verification and result validation.
8. Artifact persistence and provenance.
9. Explanation without private chain-of-thought.
10. Memory update from authorized, verified outcomes.
11. Observability, evaluation and regression recording.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','21b3f271062215c7'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Capability expansion order','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Capability expansion order": 1. Stabilize capability registry and contracts.
2. Complete universal context, intent and evidence structures.
3. Complete truth decision integration.
4. Complete memory/provenance controls.
5. Build the Skill Fabric.
6. Connect existing agents to shared Fresh AI contracts.
7. Complete Search + Research + citations.
8. Complete Files + Vision + Camera.
9. Complete Create across image/avatar/video/audio/3D with real engine boundaries.
10. Complete Code + Data + project workspace execution.
11. Complete Work + approvals + rollback + verification.
12. Complete Tasks + Automations + notifications.
13. Complete Apps/connectors with explicit scopes and audit trails.
14. Complete evaluation, safety and production observability across every capability.
15. Expand the trained fresh-unified-1 checkpoint only after these contracts are stable.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','f3b5d1d27a1afe51'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Training gate','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Training gate": Training is downstream of the product/runtime contract. The current model boundary intentionally reports training-required for the Fresh checkpoint. No document or UI may imply that a trained foundation-model checkpoint exists until an actual checkpoint is registered, loaded and verified.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','14355c761a34ef6f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Provider rule','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Provider rule": External model providers may exist only as explicit optional tool/compute adapters. They must not be required for Fresh AI core boot, reasoning, planning, memory, truth decisions, capability resolution or product identity. Provider-specific calls must never be hidden inside agents or product features.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','d17cb6ee0050bf59'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP — Definition of production-complete','Per docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md (Fresh AI Runtime Roadmap (#TRUEMODE)), section "Definition of production-complete": A capability is complete only when its typed contract, implementation, permissions, verification, tests, observability and truthful failure/degraded behavior are present. A button alone is not an implementation.','docs/FRESH_AI_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md','ce7863c0d2648a60'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Mission','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Mission": Fresh AI is the platform''s native intelligence and reasoning layer. It owns intent understanding, planning, memory, evidence evaluation, reasoning, tool selection, verification, explanation and agent orchestration.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','01ffe1e90eccbbb9'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — No provider-shaped architecture','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "No provider-shaped architecture": Fresh application code MUST NOT require ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, or another external model API key for Fresh AI''s core operation. Provider-specific SDK calls must not be embedded in agents or product features.
Fresh AI may use local algorithms, deterministic engines, indexed knowledge, platform tools, search/retrieval systems and optional compute adapters. Any optional external computation is a tool boundary, never the identity of Fresh AI and never a prerequisite for the core platform contract.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','5cf80e4726eddfd1'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Core intelligence layers (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Core intelligence layers": 1. Intent Engine — understands goals, constraints, ambiguity and desired outcomes.
2. Context Engine — gathers current task context, user-authorized memory and relevant platform state.
3. Reasoning Engine — decomposition, deduction, induction, causal analysis, counterfactuals, constraint solving and planning.
4. Knowledge Engine — structured knowledge, semantic retrieval, entity relationships and temporal state.
5. Truth Decision Orchestrator — evidence, provenance, confidence, contradiction handling, temporal truth and action boundaries.
6. Planning Engine — converts goals into executable plans, dependencies, checkpoints and rollback paths.
7. Tool Engine — selects and invokes approved platform capabilities.
8. Verification Engine — tests claims, calculations, code, changes and action results.
9. Memory Engine — stores and retrieves user-authorized durable context, project state and learned preferences.
10. Explanation Engine — reports reasoning outcomes, evidence, uncertainty and actions without exposing private chain-of-thought.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','53f1ed62185bf3bf'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Core intelligence layers (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Core intelligence layers": 11. Learning/Adaptation Engine — improves routing, retrieval and task strategies from explicit feedback and verified outcomes.
12. Safety Boundary — authorization, privacy, financial controls and destructive-action confirmation remain outside the intelligence layer and cannot be overridden by it.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','fd219c0a718946cb'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Capability fabric','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Capability fabric": Fresh AI capabilities are composable skills, not isolated chatbots:
- reasoning and analysis
- mathematics and statistics
- code generation/review/debugging
- architecture and database design
- UI/UX and design systems
- research and synthesis
- multilingual understanding/translation
- document and data analysis
- security analysis and threat modeling
- optimization
- media/audio/video understanding
- creative writing and transformation
- scientific reasoning
- simulation planning
- robotics reasoning and motion-planning algorithms
- forecasting and scenario analysis
- accessibility transformation
- education and tutoring
Where a capability requires heavy numerical simulation, rendering, model inference or specialized computation, Fresh AI owns the task and verification contract while delegating computation to an approved engine. It must never pretend a computation was performed when it was not.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','97e605845891699c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Agents','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Agents": Agents remain operational managers. They receive goals from Fresh AI, execute within explicit permissions, return evidence/results, and are verified by Fresh AI.
Examples:
- Wallet Agent
- Feed Agent
- Security Agent
- Research Agent
- Architecture Agent
- Backend Agent
- Frontend Agent
- Testing Agent
- Documentation Agent
- Deployment Agent
- Media/Shorts Agent
- Marketplace Agent
- Academy Agent
Agents MUST NOT create their own incompatible reasoning or memory systems. They consume shared Fresh AI contracts.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','2578d9c55f4012bc'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Sovereign execution loop','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Sovereign execution loop": User goal
→ intent
→ context
→ evidence
→ plan
→ skill composition
→ agent/tool execution
→ verification
→ truth decision
→ authorized action
→ observe result
→ memory update
→ explanation','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','68e5fc56ead5b1c2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — #TRUEMODE behavior','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "#TRUEMODE behavior": Fresh AI should optimize for human agency rather than engagement or apparent certainty.
For important claims and decisions it distinguishes:
- KNOWN
- SUPPORTED
- PROBABLE
- UNCERTAIN
- CONTRADICTED
- UNKNOWN
- BLOCKED
It must preserve conflicting evidence rather than silently deleting it. It must retain temporal context where relevant. It must say when information is missing.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','8a6b4708d11af7d2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Native does not mean magical','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Native does not mean magical": “API-keyless Fresh AI” means Fresh''s product contract, orchestration, reasoning algorithms, memory, knowledge, tools and verification do not depend on users supplying third-party AI keys. It does not mean every advanced computation is implemented from scratch in browser JavaScript. Heavy capabilities are modular engines behind Fresh-owned interfaces.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','c8a0f04e32795367'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Billion-developer quality bar','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Billion-developer quality bar": The architecture must favor:
- typed contracts
- deterministic fallbacks
- observability
- provenance
- reproducibility
- unit/integration/e2e tests
- capability versioning
- permission boundaries
- graceful degradation
- offline/local operation where practical
- explicit uncertainty
- no fabricated tool results
- no hidden provider coupling
- backward-compatible skill interfaces','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','488fc27befefd241'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE — Implementation rule','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh AI — Sovereign Intelligence Architecture (#TRUEMODE)), section "Implementation rule": Build the intelligence substrate first, then migrate agents and product surfaces to it. Do not replace working product behavior with placeholder AI screens. Every capability must have a real implementation boundary, tests, and a clear fallback when its required computation is unavailable.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_INTELLIGENCE.md','68d9c1949d45235b'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — North star','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "North star": Fresh AI is the platform''s sovereign intelligence layer. Core reasoning must function without a ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, or other provider API key. Platform agents remain operational managers and execute specialized workflows through Fresh AI.
This does not mean pretending that every scientific or computational capability is magically available in one model. Fresh AI owns the intelligence interface, reasoning, memory, truth boundary, planning and orchestration; native algorithms, local engines, Fresh services and explicitly permitted tools provide concrete computation.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','5c893df26cc8f4d5'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 1 — Native Intelligence Core','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 1 — Native Intelligence Core": - Intent understanding
- Context assembly
- Symbolic and semantic reasoning
- Planning and decomposition
- Constraint solving
- Causal and counterfactual reasoning
- Confidence calibration
- Unknown detection
- Contradiction preservation
- Explanation generation','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','855a0bbda139277f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 2 — Truth and Knowledge Fabric','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 2 — Truth and Knowledge Fabric": - Evidence records
- Claim extraction
- Source provenance
- Temporal validity
- Knowledge graph
- Contradiction graph
- Confidence model
- Known/probable/uncertain/contradicted/unknown/blocked states
- Truth Decision Orchestrator','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','f75a79a8dbad2653'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 3 — Universal Memory','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 3 — Universal Memory": - Personal memory
- Cross-app memory
- Project memory
- Media memory
- Conversation memory
- Preference memory
- Explicit forget controls
- Memory provenance and correction','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','e4d99d15039bf012'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 4 — Skill Fabric','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 4 — Skill Fabric": Fresh AI composes reusable skills rather than duplicating reasoning inside agents:
intent → skill discovery → composition → plan → reason → verify → act → observe → learn
Initial skill domains include reasoning, research, code, architecture, UI/UX, mathematics, science, security, media, data analysis, translation, optimization, learning and automation.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','b6458bdca3dd35d4'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 5 — Platform Agents','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 5 — Platform Agents": - Wallet Agent
- Feed Agent
- Security Agent
- Research Agent
- Architecture Agent
- Backend Agent
- Frontend Agent
- Testing Agent
- Documentation Agent
- Deployment Agent
- Media Agent
- Learning Agent
Agents coordinate work. They do not become separate AI providers.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','4f5af6a2a3ddb9ba'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 6 — Native creation and engineering','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 6 — Native creation and engineering": Fresh AI should understand and operate on Fresh projects as structured systems:
- repository inspection
- code generation and review
- database/schema reasoning
- UI/component generation
- test generation
- performance analysis
- security analysis
- deployment planning
- media creation and transformation','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','04fce9c7e58c88f3'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 7 — Scientific and analytical domains','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 7 — Scientific and analytical domains": Provide native reasoning and tool interfaces for mathematics, statistics, physics, chemistry, biology, simulation planning, forecasting and data analysis. Domain-specific high-compute tasks must be routed to concrete engines/tools rather than falsely represented as pure language reasoning.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','acae93b03198f3c9'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 8 — #TRUEMODE safety and agency','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 8 — #TRUEMODE safety and agency": - Explain why a decision was made.
- Show evidence where available.
- Preserve disagreement.
- Admit unknowns.
- Never fabricate provenance.
- Require approval at sensitive action boundaries.
- Keep financial authorization behind the trusted Treasury boundary.
- Let users inspect, correct and forget memory.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','8058bf771587bec7'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Layer 9 — Evaluation','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Layer 9 — Evaluation": Every capability needs:
- unit tests
- integration tests
- end-to-end tests
- adversarial tests
- regression corpus
- truth/calibration benchmarks
- latency/resource measurements
- agent-action safety tests','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','38911187f54892a6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Implementation order','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Implementation order": 1. Stabilize FreshIntelligenceEngine interfaces.
2. Build native context + intent + claim/evidence structures.
3. Implement Truth Decision Orchestrator.
4. Implement memory fabric and provenance.
5. Implement Skill Fabric.
6. Connect existing agents to the engine.
7. Add native engineering and media capabilities.
8. Add scientific/computational tool interfaces.
9. Build evaluation harness and production observability.
10. Expand capabilities without changing the sovereign contract.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','3b17622bbef3cb42'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP — Non-negotiable API-key rule','Per docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md (#TRUEMODE — Fresh AI Sovereign Intelligence Roadmap), section "Non-negotiable API-key rule": The Fresh AI core must boot, reason over its available local/contextual inputs, explain, plan and coordinate without provider API keys. Optional external tools may exist only behind explicit adapters and must never become a hidden dependency of core Fresh AI behavior.','docs/FRESH_AI_SOVEREIGN_ROADMAP.md','ceb5622385bfbe23'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC — Purpose','Per docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md (Fresh AI Universal Power Fabric), section "Purpose": Fresh AI keeps the powers already present across the Fresh AI architecture while moving them behind one canonical capability contract.
The migration principle is transfer, normalize, combine — do not discard.','docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md','e9f2815ddd765dfb'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC — Canonical power domains','Per docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md (Fresh AI Universal Power Fabric), section "Canonical power domains": - Understanding
- Conversation
- Knowledge & Search
- Reasoning
- Memory
- Creation
- Action & Agents
- Communication
- Media Intelligence
- Engineering
- Automation
- Verification & Truth
- Safety & Governance','docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md','e757a8498290c657'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC — Migration rule','Per docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md (Fresh AI Universal Power Fabric), section "Migration rule": Existing implementations remain usable while adapters move their capabilities into the canonical fabric. No existing capability should be removed merely because a duplicate contract exists.
The fabric is a capability contract and resolver. It does not claim that every listed provider is already production-wired.','docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md','a996952dd531df9a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC — Governance','Per docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md (Fresh AI Universal Power Fabric), section "Governance": The fabric never silently approves an action requiring approval. Execution remains behind the existing Fresh AI gateway, ARA6 and verification boundaries.','docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md','a8eb1b17c1ce310c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC — Verification','Per docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md (Fresh AI Universal Power Fabric), section "Verification": node scripts/verify-fresh-ai-power-fabric.mjs checks that the canonical power set, resolver, normalization and integrity verifier exist and that Fresh AI Everywhere points at the canonical gateway contract.','docs/FRESH_AI_UNIVERSAL_POWER_FABRIC.md','4ac716269f32e759'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE — Thesis','Per docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh Beyond Superintelligence), section "Thesis": Superintelligence, as commonly marketed, means more cognitive power.
Fresh is built to be more than that: a sovereign intelligence system for:
 · Pillar · Meaning · 
 · Truth · Known / probable / uncertain / contradicted / blocked — not fluent bluffing · 
 · Agency · Plans and tools with approvals for high-impact actions · 
 · Memory · Useful context without silent leakage of private life · 
 · Creation · Text, image, 3D, code, media under one model identity · 
 · Work · Intelligence inside the product the user already uses · 
 · Privacy · Client at-rest seal; honest limits on server-side inference · 
 · Learning · Authorized data, hashed checkpoints, evaluation before promotion · 
 · Governance · Bounded self-improvement proposals; no autonomous production mutation ·','docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md','821da363289b6dd6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE — What we do not claim','Per docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh Beyond Superintelligence), section "What we do not claim": - AGI or ASI achieved
- Finished foundation weights (weightsStatus: training-required)
- Server-blind E2EE while cloud inference is required
- Autonomous code/policy/deploy changes','docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md','c1b9027c6e1a83d0'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE — Code','Per docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh Beyond Superintelligence), section "Code": - Contract: src/core/fresh-ai/FreshBeyondSuperintelligence.ts
- Truth: semanticTruthEngine, FreshTruthDecisionOrchestrator
- Bounded ASI: asi.ts
- Training evidence: training/STARTERRUN1.md
- Privacy: src/core/crypto/, vault UI, seal-latest API','docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md','13b7d5e2a9378662'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE — Product bar','Per docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md (Fresh Beyond Superintelligence), section "Product bar": A system that is only "smarter text" is incomplete for Fresh.
Fresh ships when truth + work + privacy + creation + governed action move together — with honest training status until promotion gates pass.','docs/FRESH_BEYOND_SUPERINTELLIGENCE.md','ba1e5c78cd02736a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal": Status: Proposed architecture; not production implementation 
Owner identity: Fresh ID 
Product: Fresh Web Lite / Fresh Communication 
Principle: One communication home, one identity, connected history and search, purpose-built delivery systems behind it.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','b7ddd6da7dfb5138'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Executive recommendation','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Executive recommendation": Yes: the entire communication experience should live inside Fresh. A user should not need to jump between separate Fresh Mail, chat, notifications, calls, and AI screens to understand or continue a conversation.
Unify the user experience, identity, navigation, discovery, privacy controls, and conversation context. Do not force email, real-time chat, voice/video, push notifications, and AI sessions into one giant table or one transport. Those systems have different delivery, retention, security, and reliability requirements.
Fresh Communication should be the shared product shell over specialized, permissioned services and adapters.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','6c74e29bd37f942f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 1. The user-facing product (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "1. The user-facing product": A single top-level destination: Fresh Communication.
- Unified Inbox — one chronological view of new activity, with filters for Email, Direct, Groups, Calls, Notifications, and AI. Users can choose combined or separate views.
- Conversations — one thread view where an internal discussion can link to an email, a call, a shared file, or an AI-generated summary without pretending these are identical message types.
- Fresh Mail — external email addresses, inbox, sent, drafts, replies, attachments, folders/labels, spam, archive, and delivery states.
- Direct & Group Chat — internal Fresh-to-Fresh messages, typing/presence when online, read receipts as opt-in, group membership and moderation.
- Calls & Voice — voice notes first; real-time audio/video later after network, device, privacy, and cost testing.
- Notifications — one preference center, with quiet hours, per-channel controls, and a digest; no engagement-bait defaults.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','643084be3881f350'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 1. The user-facing product (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "1. The user-facing product": - Fresh AI — optional summarization, search, drafting, translation, and action suggestions, always clearly marked as AI-generated and never silently sending a message.
- Files & shared items — a conversation-scoped view of attachments, links, and documents, governed by the source conversation''s permissions.
The UI should be mobile-first, work on small and low-memory Android devices, use readable text and large touch targets, support keyboard/screen readers, and avoid requiring horizontal swiping to discover essential controls. Users should be able to hide channels they do not use.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','42dc0977d51700f6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 2. Identity and addressing','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "2. Identity and addressing": Fresh ID is the account identity and authorization source. Communication addresses are distinct, verified identifiers attached to that account:
- Fresh ID username — internal discovery and direct messages.
- Fresh Mail address — an externally routable email address on a domain Fresh controls.
- Optional contact methods — phone or other verified channels only if/when implemented.
Do not automatically expose a user''s email address, phone number, date of birth, or real name to other users. Users need explicit controls for discoverability, address visibility, blocking, and who may message them.
Do not promise an address until domain/provider verification and mailbox provisioning succeed. A Fresh username is not automatically an email address.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','2c06bcfb47c7a349'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — A. Product shell','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "A. Product shell": One navigation entry and consistent conversation UI. The shell requests only data the signed-in user is allowed to see. The combined inbox is a presentation/query layer, not a reason to grant broad cross-table access.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','57cdc0547a17b7d5'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — B. Communication directory and thread index','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "B. Communication directory and thread index": A minimal common index for participants, channel type, display title, last-activity time, unread state, and links to the underlying source records. It must not duplicate private message bodies just to make the inbox fast.
Every index entry must have a source type, source ID, visibility/participant model, and authorization check. Rebuildable indexes should not become the authority for access decisions.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','18dce38add2680be'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — C. Purpose-built data stores','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "C. Purpose-built data stores": - Internal direct/group messages remain distinct from external email.
- Email records keep envelope sender/recipients, headers, provider message IDs, threading identifiers, delivery events, normalized body, and attachment references.
- Calls store call/session metadata and participant permissions; recording is off by default and requires clear consent/legal review.
- AI session records are distinct from human messages, with explicit user controls for whether they may be used for summaries or suggestions.
- Notifications are delivery pointers and preferences, not copied full message bodies.
Reuse existing FWL tables only after validating their schema and authorization behavior. In particular, audit directmessages, freshcommunicationthreads, and freshcommunication_messages before extending them. Do not retrofit email into the existing internal-message table.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','7c7192a6ffb5c93e'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — D. Provider adapters and event processing (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "D. Provider adapters and event processing": External email provider integration lives behind a server-side adapter. Client apps never receive provider secrets.
- Outbound: authenticated compose request → authorization and abuse/quota checks → durable send job/outbox → provider API → delivery/bounce events → status visible in Fresh.
- Inbound: provider webhook → signature/timestamp verification → idempotency/replay check → recipient/mailbox mapping → durable message and attachment metadata → inbox index/notification.
- Retries use bounded backoff and idempotency keys. A webhook may be delivered more than once; processing must not create duplicate messages.
- Provider outages must not erase drafts or make Fresh claim a message was delivered when it was only queued.
- Store provider IDs and delivery events so a provider can be changed later without losing the user''s mailbox history.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','8d9910906e37bdc2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — D. Provider adapters and event processing (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "D. Provider adapters and event processing": The first provider candidate is Resend for a proof of concept because its documented inbound model includes webhooks, receiving APIs, and attachment retrieval. This is not a final selection: validate current plan limits, retention, domain support, and full cost first. Mailgun and Amazon SES remain alternatives.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','dfc63d53201efaf2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 4. Security and privacy boundaries (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "4. Security and privacy boundaries": - Supabase Auth/Fresh ID owns authentication; authorization is enforced by database policies and server routes, not UI visibility alone.
- Never place Supabase service-role/secret keys or mail-provider API keys in browser code, public environment variables, logs, or AI prompts.
- Every operation must authorize both the actor and the target mailbox/thread. Knowing a UUID must never grant access.
- Enable RLS on exposed tables and verify effective grants as well as policies. RLS does not make a broadly granted table safe by itself.
- Validate provider webhook signatures against the raw request body using the provider''s documented scheme; reject invalid signatures and replays.
- Private attachments belong in private storage, with short-lived authorized downloads; public buckets are inappropriate for private mail.
- Protect against spam, spoofing, phishing, oversized messages, malicious attachments, HTML email tracking, and abusive sending. Sanitize/render HTML email safely and load remote images only under an explicit privacy policy.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','a918eaf3018576b7'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 4. Security and privacy boundaries (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "4. Security and privacy boundaries": - Minimize logs: IDs, timings, provider status, and safe error codes by default; do not log message bodies, access tokens, or attachments.
- Provide block/report, spam handling, rate limits, quotas, account recovery, export, deletion, and retention policies.
- Keep sensitive profile data such as DOB separate from public communication profiles.
- AI features are opt-in and permission-scoped. AI must not search or summarize a thread the current user cannot read, and must not send or forward without explicit confirmation.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','0a406b4c042e7ff5'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 5. Reliability and delivery truth','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "5. Reliability and delivery truth": Use clear, separate states:
- Draft — saved only in Fresh.
- Queued — accepted by Fresh for processing.
- Sent to provider — provider accepted the send request.
- Delivered — provider supplied delivery confirmation where available; do not infer it merely from an API success.
- Bounced / Failed — show a useful explanation and a retry path where safe.
- Received — inbound message is durably stored and mapped to the correct mailbox.
Internal chat may use its own delivery/read states. Do not label email as read just because a notification was opened; email read receipts are unreliable and privacy-sensitive.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','62b35531fcb42087'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Phase 0 — audit and acceptance criteria','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Phase 0 — audit and acceptance criteria": - Complete Fresh ID registration, email confirmation, recovery, session restore, and landing-page navigation tests.
- Verify all communication-table policies and grants, including cross-thread and cross-account negative tests.
- Review server routes, storage buckets/policies, secret handling, redirect URLs, and Supabase Auth security settings.
- Approve the domain/provider and total recurring cost only after a sandbox proof.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','1e8d3b36585324dc'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Phase 1 — secure foundation','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Phase 1 — secure foundation": - Fix verified communication authorization gaps through reviewed migrations and negative tests.
- Define common thread/index contracts without copying private message content.
- Define event idempotency, audit events, retention, deletion, quotas, and failure states.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','b18c6869de461927'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Phase 2 — first complete Fresh Mail journey','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Phase 2 — first complete Fresh Mail journey": - Verify a domain and provider in a sandbox.
- Register/claim an address only after provisioning succeeds.
- Send to an independent external account, reply back, reload, and verify both messages persist.
- Add compose, inbox, thread view, sent, drafts, attachment permissions, bounce/failure handling, and owner-isolation tests.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','5e3d4789f1dbc0e5'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Phase 3 — unified inbox','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Phase 3 — unified inbox": - Bring existing Fresh direct/group messages into the common inbox through permission-checked adapters.
- Add unread counts, search, filters, notification settings, and conversation linking.
- Preserve existing messaging behavior and migrate gradually; no destructive rewrite.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','1fb55200efd07337'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Phase 4 — calls and collaboration','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Phase 4 — calls and collaboration": - Voice notes and shared files first; then real-time voice/video, presence, and group features only after device/network and cost tests.
- Add calendar/task handoffs only with explicit user intent and permissions.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','e31a1e26ee1c9db9'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Phase 5 — AI and ecosystem integration','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Phase 5 — AI and ecosystem integration": - Summaries, translation, draft suggestions, search, and action extraction.
- Clear provenance, per-conversation opt-in, user review, and explicit confirmation before external actions.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','d1d16f3ce435dd4f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 7. MVP acceptance tests (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "7. MVP acceptance tests": 1. A newly registered user confirms email, signs in, restores their profile, and reaches the intended Fresh landing page.
2. A user cannot read or mutate another user''s private profile, thread, message, email, attachment, or delivery event by guessing IDs.
3. A user can send an external email, receive a reply from an independent account, and see both persist after reload.
4. Repeated provider webhooks do not create duplicate messages; invalid signatures are rejected.
5. Bounce, invalid recipient, rate limit, timeout, and provider outage produce truthful status and safe retry behavior.
6. Internal chat still works after unified-inbox integration, with participant/thread authorization tests passing.
7. Combined search respects the source permissions of every result and does not leak subject lines/snippets from inaccessible mail.
8. Small-screen, keyboard, screen-reader, zoom, and reduced-motion checks pass for core communication flows.
9. Export/deletion and retention behavior is documented and exercised.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','2bb5a8d75b3909f6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 7. MVP acceptance tests (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "7. MVP acceptance tests": 10. Preview and production deployments record the tested commit SHA and a rollback plan.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','5dbd4456d03641a0'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — 8. Decisions needed before paid setup','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "8. Decisions needed before paid setup": - Approve a domain name and renewal price.
- Approve a maximum monthly mail-provider budget and initial daily send quota.
- Decide whether Fresh Mail addresses are available to all users immediately or through a controlled beta.
- Confirm whether internal messages and external emails should share one default inbox (recommended) or open in separate tabs by default (filters should always remain available).','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','3646fe3b3cb9addb'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE — Final design principle','Per docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Communication — Unified Product and Architecture Proposal), section "Final design principle": One Fresh Communication experience, one Fresh ID, many permissioned communication channels. The user sees one connected system; the engineering keeps each channel reliable, auditable, and secure.','docs/FRESH_COMMUNICATION_UNIFIED_ARCHITECTURE.md','4943acc4a009f001'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO — Contract','Per docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md (Fresh Design System — Point 0), section "Contract": Design rules → tokens → primitives → icons → surfaces → ecosystems.
The design system is the platform-wide visual and interaction contract. Ecosystems consume it; they do not fork it.','docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md','25b6d4019a1faff2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO — Principles','Per docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md (Fresh Design System — Point 0), section "Principles": - Universal: one platform, personalized representation.
- Simple: expose the smallest useful interface for the current intent.
- Consistent: one meaning, one canonical pattern.
- Adaptive: device, network, language and accessibility change representation, not meaning.
- Accessible: touch, keyboard, voice, camera and assistive input are first-class.
- Fast: lightweight primitives and progressive enhancement.
- Trustworthy: permissions, states, consequences and recovery are understandable.
- Authentic: optimize for usefulness and genuine engagement.
- Extensible: new capabilities consume shared primitives.','docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md','85dfae9356e46b9a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO — Canonical contracts','Per docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md (Fresh Design System — Point 0), section "Canonical contracts": - Minimum interactive target: 44px.
- Visible focus-visible treatment is required.
- Reduced motion must be respected.
- Icon-only controls require an accessible name.
- Essential meaning must not depend on color alone.
- Native HTML semantics come before ARIA.
- Primary content flows are vertical by default on small screens.
- Public startup branding is Fresh Web Lite; personal identity belongs in Fresh ID/Profile/Personal Space.','docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md','c813d26e40d0e7a6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO — Icon policy','Per docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md (Fresh Design System — Point 0), section "Icon policy": src/core/design/icons/registry.ts owns semantic meaning. src/components/Icons.tsx remains a compatibility surface until consumers are migrated. New icons must be added to the registry first and must not introduce synonymous meanings.','docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md','96f87ab940d49450'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO — Surface policy','Per docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md (Fresh Design System — Point 0), section "Surface policy": Advanced capability should remain discoverable without overwhelming the default experience. Implementation details, secrets and internal architecture never become user-facing UI.','docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md','1abf87e934411c2a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO — Evolution','Per docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md (Fresh Design System — Point 0), section "Evolution": Token changes are global changes. Primitive changes must preserve semantic meaning across ecosystems. Ecosystem-specific styling is allowed only when it does not create a competing visual language.','docs/FRESH_DESIGN_SYSTEM_POINT_ZERO.md','6ff42782e56c8523'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE — Three layers','Per docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Flow — Media Operating Architecture), section "Three layers": · Layer · Question · Surface rule · 
 · A · Media Director · What am I consuming? · Flow Switch — summoned, never permanent six-tile chrome · 
 · B · Discovery Director · How is content selected? · Contextual chips per world · 
 · C · Content Experience · How do I interact? · Contextual; collapses when idle · 
Design law: the interface must never expose the entire architecture merely because the architecture exists.','docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md','1c8a0f2f95229d82'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE — Six media worlds','Per docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Flow — Media Operating Architecture), section "Six media worlds": · World · Surface · Route · 
 · Fresh Short · Immersive vertical · fresh-flow · 
 · Long Videos · Cinematic player · fresh-flow-long-videos · 
 · News / Posts · Information · fresh-flow-news-posts · 
 · VR / AR · Environment · fresh-flow-ar-vr · 
 · Podcasts · Audio-first · fresh-flow-podcasts · 
 · Others · Emerging formats · fresh-flow-more · 
Each world defines its own discovery modes (For You, Trending, Learn, …) in src/features/fresh-flow/core/freshFlowArchitecture.ts.','docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md','81e3a5c756fcc9e8'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE — Universal services (cross-world)','Per docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Flow — Media Operating Architecture), section "Universal services (cross-world)": Search · Voice · Translate · Share · Save · History · Follow · Notifications · Fresh AI
These stay global; they are not duplicated as permanent chrome inside every world.','docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md','d7d0ae32ade579ab'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE — Code map','Per docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Flow — Media Operating Architecture), section "Code map": · Piece · Path · 
 · Architecture source of truth · core/freshFlowArchitecture.ts · 
 · Flow Switch (Layer A UI) · components/FreshFlowSwitch.tsx · 
 · Hub shell · FreshFlowHub.tsx · 
 · Short experience · components/FreshFlowShortsExperience.tsx · 
 · Long / VR / Pod / Others workspace · components/FreshFlowMediaWorkspace.tsx · 
 · News / Posts · components/FreshFlowNewsPosts.tsx ·','docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md','52f2878ada77c68c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE — UX sequence (Short entry)','Per docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md (Fresh Flow — Media Operating Architecture), section "UX sequence (Short entry)": 1. 0–5s — content only (minimal UI)
2. Content settled — discovery + interaction appear contextually
3. User summons Flow Switch when changing media world
Fresh Short remains the immersive entry; Fresh Flow remains the larger media universe.','docs/FRESH_FLOW_MEDIA_ARCHITECTURE.md','c50af66462620bf0'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — Purpose','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "Purpose": Fresh should understand the world as a connected, multilingual, time-aware evidence graph rather than as a flat collection of text. Wikidata is the first international structured-knowledge intake candidate because its official documentation states that structured data in the main, Property, Lexeme and EntitySchema namespaces is released under CC0. This is an intake candidate, not an automatic production-training approval.','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','5528eb98e80f9b03'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — Design principles (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "Design principles": 1. International by default — knowledge must support countries, languages, cultures, institutions and domains beyond a single national perspective.
2. Graph first, text second — structured entities and relationships are first-class objects; text is supporting evidence, not the graph itself.
3. Evidence attached to claims — every consequential claim should retain source and provenance information when available.
4. Temporal truth — facts can have start/end validity and must not be treated as timeless.
5. Contradiction is data — conflicting claims are preserved and evaluated; they are not silently overwritten.
6. Multilingual identity — one entity can have many language labels and aliases without becoming multiple entities.
7. Jurisdiction aware — laws, standards, rights and other jurisdiction-sensitive claims retain their jurisdiction.
8. No blind trust — graph membership does not equal truth. Fresh''s truth layer evaluates evidence, independence, provenance, temporal validity and confidence before consequential action.','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','d64b58a01954dfac'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — Design principles (part 2/2)','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "Design principles": 9. Fresh-owned semantic layer — external sources enrich the graph, but Fresh maintains its own canonical IDs, mappings, provenance and validation state.
10. Rights-aware ingestion — source licensing and acquisition rights remain attached to every imported dataset/version.','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','54dd5dc86e27127f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — V1 entity model','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "V1 entity model": Minimum entity types:
- Person
- Organization
- Place
- Country / territory
- Language
- Work / creative work
- Scientific concept
- Event
- Product / technology
- Software
- Dataset
- Institution
- Species / biological entity
- Legal / regulatory concept
- Time period
- Measurement / unit
Minimum relationship types:
- instance-of
- subclass-of
- part-of
- located-in
- member-of
- founded-by
- owned-by
- created-by
- developed-by
- based-on
- related-to
- predecessor-of
- successor-of
- occurs-at
- occurs-during
- uses-language
- has-license
- governed-by
- cited-by
- supports
- contradicts','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','dcd9b763029b1ff8'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — Claim record','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "Claim record": A Fresh claim should be representable as:
subject -> predicate -> object/value
with optional:
- claim ID
- source IDs
- reference URLs
- source publication/observation date
- valid-from / valid-until
- jurisdiction
- language
- provenance chain
- confidence
- validation status
- supporting claim IDs
- counter-evidence IDs
- contradiction group
- last verified timestamp','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','5ccbd669f67a71e5'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — Wikidata V1 role','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "Wikidata V1 role": Wikidata should initially serve as an international structured knowledge foundation, not as Fresh''s final worldview and not as an automatic model-training corpus.
Use the official dump/data-access routes for large-scale acquisition rather than uncontrolled live scraping. Record the exact dataset version, acquisition date, source URL, file hash, transformation version and license evidence.
The imported graph should be normalized into Fresh''s own schema so that Fresh can later combine:
- Wikidata structured knowledge
- directly licensed professional datasets
- authoritative institutional sources
- Fresh-owned knowledge
- user-authorized private knowledge
- Fresh research observations
without making any source inherently authoritative.','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','77463e98fce0032a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — Training versus knowledge graph','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "Training versus knowledge graph": The knowledge graph and the model-training corpus are separate assets.
- Knowledge graph: continuously updateable, source-linked, multilingual, temporal and queryable.
- Training corpus: versioned, legally authorized, privacy/safety/quality reviewed and explicitly promoted.
- Model weights: trained only from approved training data.
A graph update must never silently become a model-training update.','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','1279b41b66e53a52'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1 — V1 gate','Per docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md (Fresh International Knowledge Graph V1), section "V1 gate": The Wikidata candidate is currently blocked from production promotion until Fresh completes legal review and corpus privacy, safety, quality and deduplication checks. No external source bytes are claimed to have been acquired by this commit.','docs/FRESH_INTERNATIONAL_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_V1.md','699479e25d229570'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow": Fresh, cohesive product powers for a next-generation platform that can challenge Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, and RedNote — grounded in Fresh Web Lite / Fresh Flow doctrine: useful + authentic first, human agency preserved.
This document is the product-facing companion to FRESHWEBLITEUNIVERSALPLATFORMDOCTRINE.md. Doctrine answers why and how we build; this answers what powers users feel every day*.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','29c774cf1b8cbfd1'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 1. Core Philosophy: Useful + Authentic First','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "1. Core Philosophy: Useful + Authentic First": The platform is built on high-trust, actionable content rather than pure entertainment or envy. Every post is designed to be save-worthy and re-creatable. Users come to discover real experiences, practical guides, honest reviews, budgets, routes, and tips — not just scroll for dopamine.
Fresh principles:
- Authentic engagement over virality
- Value created per meaningful interaction
- True before impressive
- Anti-addiction design by default','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','b4feb870453ab7f6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 2. Discovery Engine: Search + Interest Graph Hybrid','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "2. Discovery Engine: Search + Interest Graph Hybrid": - Powerful search that works like a lifestyle search engine (places, products, how-tos, local tips).
- Interest-based recommendation that surfaces content by usefulness, not just follower count or virality.
- Heavy weighting on saves, deep comments, and shares so valuable posts stay visible for months or years.
- Visual masonry grid + short video + longer notes so content serves both quick browsing and deep reference.
- Built-in maps and local discovery: see nearby notes, get directions, and explore real places through authentic user experiences.
Fresh mapping: Fresh Flow discovery tabs (For You, Trending, Following, Fresh Picks), universal search, knowledge graph, and ranking that favors durable utility over 24–48 hour decay.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','d069e218c74a5303'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 3. Content Creation: Low Barrier, High Utility','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "3. Content Creation: Low Barrier, High Utility": - Easy tools for photo carousels, short vertical video, longer video, text notes, live, and audio.
- Strong emphasis on authentic, non-polished content while still supporting high production.
- Anti-gatekeeping culture: creators are rewarded for sharing exact details (costs, locations, steps) so others can recreate the experience.
- Content that ranks in search long-term instead of disappearing in 24–48 hours.
Fresh mapping: Creator Studio, Shorts create FAB, remix / duet / edit / captions / effects handoff, True Mode video tools, multi-format Fresh Flow directorates (Shorts, Long Videos, News/Posts, AR/VR, Podcasts).','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','0952b2a2baa0f094'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 4. Social Layer: Real Connection Over Broadcast','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "4. Social Layer: Real Connection Over Broadcast": - Mix of public discovery feeds and tight-knit groups, interest rooms, and private/semi-private spaces.
- Features that encourage genuine conversation (deep comments, Q&A, collaborative notes) instead of passive likes.
- Friends and real-world connections remain visible and prioritized when users want them.
- Location-aware and community-driven discovery so people connect around shared places and interests.
Fresh mapping: Fresh ID social graph, follows, comments, reactions, collaborative create intents, communities as first-class ecosystems — not broadcast-only timelines.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','ba2c91de8ca9b11c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 5. Creator Economy: Ownership & Fair Pay','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "5. Creator Economy: Ownership & Fair Pay": - Transparent, higher revenue share plus direct fan payments, tipping, subscriptions, and commerce cuts.
- Small and mid-tier creators can earn meaningfully without needing massive follower counts.
- Portable data and follower graphs so creators aren’t locked into one platform.
- Native shopping that feels like natural discovery (soft seeding through authentic reviews and experiences) rather than hard-sell ads.
Fresh mapping: Fresh Wallet, gifts on Shorts, Creator Studio analytics from live data, portable Fresh ID, interoperability and export as doctrine — not lock-in.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','acc91546ca279c5e'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 6. User Control & Trust Layer','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "6. User Control & Trust Layer": - Choose chronological, friends-only, interest-based, or full algorithmic feed.
- Strong privacy defaults, clear data controls, and optional end-to-end encryption.
- Tools to limit time spent, hide vanity metrics, and filter polarizing content.
- Transparent moderation with clear appeals — reducing arbitrary bans while still protecting the community.
- Design that reduces addiction loops and prioritizes mental well-being.
Fresh mapping: Feed mode controls, Fresh AI E2EE strategy, privacy by architecture, trust layer (true before impressive), anti-addiction metrics, human-centered governance.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','e968a858b73a8042'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — 7. Seamless Utility + Commerce','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "7. Seamless Utility + Commerce": - Shopping, maps, itineraries, product comparisons, and real-world tools live inside the experience.
- High-intent discovery (users come ready to research and act) combined with trusted peer recommendations.
- Commerce feels helpful rather than intrusive.
Fresh mapping: Search → knowledge → action; wallet and commerce as utility; intent → context → action → outcome (Personal Digital OS), not app → screen → feature.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','eb2246285a4298a2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — Overall User Flow','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "Overall User Flow": The combination: RedNote-style usefulness and trust + TikTok-level discovery power + stronger creator economics + genuine user control — a platform that feels both more practical and more human than the current giants.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','805a180fb79285be'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — How this challenges the giants','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "How this challenges the giants": · Giant · Weakness Fresh targets · 
 · Facebook · Broadcast + engagement max; weak high-trust utility · 
 · Instagram · Aesthetic envy loops; limited durable how-to value · 
 · TikTok · Extreme short-term virality; weak long-term search utility · 
 · YouTube · Strong long-form, weaker lifestyle search + local authenticity · 
 · RedNote · Strong utility culture; Fresh adds broader media + creator ownership + agency · 
Fresh does not win by copying one feed. It wins by making useful, authentic, controllable, creator-fair discovery the default product loop.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','aacc1bc2e4e75cd9'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW — Implementation anchors (codebase)','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md (Fresh Platform Powers & User Flow), section "Implementation anchors (codebase)": · Power · Primary surfaces · 
 · Discovery · FreshFlowHub, ranking (ForYouRanking, FreshFlowRanking), search surface · 
 · Short-form · FreshFlowShortsExperience (5s → immersive), FreshFlowShortsStream · 
 · Create · Creator Studio, create intent sessionStorage, edit tools · 
 · Trust / privacy · Fresh ID, E2EE docs, production gates · 
 · Economy · Wallet, gifts, creator analytics · 
 · Doctrine · docs/FRESHWEBLITEUNIVERSALPLATFORMDOCTRINE.md · 
Build it true. Build it useful. Build it universal. Build it for humanity.**','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_POWERS_AND_USER_FLOW.md','927c78c6a2da72ae'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_RUNTIME_EXPANSION — Fresh Platform Runtime Expansion','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_RUNTIME_EXPANSION.md (Fresh Platform Runtime Expansion), section "Fresh Platform Runtime Expansion": Implemented runtime paths now shared across Fresh Flow, Studio and future backend adapters:
- Recommendation: weighted reranking plus optional embedding cosine similarity. The existing formula remains the base ranking model; semantic similarity can be added without requiring a vector database.
- Realtime: Supabase Realtime broadcast transport is executable in-browser. WebSocket transport remains available for a dedicated gateway.
- Media pipeline: jobs now have stage progress and a resumable runner. AI stages remain adapter points until real inference services are deployed.
- Playback: Studio already persists position/rate in IndexedDB and supports 0.05x controls through 3x.
- Studio → Creator → Flow: existing session handoff and canonical publishing repository remain the publishing path.
- Escrow: state transitions now validate inputs and support explicit refund state. This is a ledger state machine, not a payment processor.
- Browser AI: Web Speech Recognition is an optional local transcription capability. It is a browser fallback, not a Whisper replacement.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_RUNTIME_EXPANSION.md','762199312cea7e9c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_PLATFORM_RUNTIME_EXPANSION — Production boundary','Per docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_RUNTIME_EXPANSION.md (Fresh Platform Runtime Expansion), section "Production boundary": Not claimed as deployed by this change:
FFmpeg GPU clusters, Demucs/S3T, YOLO/MediaPipe, Whisper, NMT/TTS voice cloning, HLS/DASH packaging, Redis/Kafka, WebRTC media backend, vector database, Stripe/smart-contract settlement, copyright fingerprinting.
Those require external runtime services and should plug into the interfaces already established here.','docs/FRESH_PLATFORM_RUNTIME_EXPANSION.md','75a697fb20e8fdeb'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP — Fresh powers and missions map','Per docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md (Fresh powers and missions map), section "Fresh powers and missions map": Audit date: 2026-10-12. Nothing here removes a power, ecosystem or system. Each
item is sorted, matched to the code and database that carries it, and given an
honest status. "Wired" means confirmed in api/ai/ask.ts. "Declared" means the
power exists in FreshAIUniversalPowerFabric.ts but runtime use is unverified.','docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md','14320600c730916f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP — 1. The 14 powers, matched to the master matrix (part 1/2)','Per docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md (Fresh powers and missions map), section "1. The 14 powers, matched to the master matrix": · Power · Matrix ecosystems · Code anchor · Status · 
