 ('Doc: FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP — 4. Missions','Per docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md (Fresh powers and missions map), section "4. Missions": src/core/fresh-ai/mission/missionManager.ts is in-memory and resets on every
serverless cold start. It is untouched. missionStore.ts (new) persists missions
to freshaimissions with per-user RLS. Each mission can carry an ecosystem
and a power so it ties back to this map.','docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md','0fef847ec6571427'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP — 5. Training Fresh AI','Per docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md (Fresh powers and missions map), section "5. Training Fresh AI": Two different things share the name:
1. Live Fresh AI: a Gemini-backed gateway. It improves through grounding data,
 not weights. This audit seeds freshaicapabilities (14), freshaiknowledge
 (74 platform facts: 16 hand-written + 58 generated from the master matrix) and freshaitrainingexamples (instruction, safety,
 preference and evaluation examples) and makes api/ai/ask.ts retrieve from
 freshaiknowledge.
2. fresh-unified-1: the from-scratch model. It is at pipeline smoke-test stage
 (46 synthetic examples). It needs a large authorized corpus and GPUs before it
 is useful. The seed deliberately does not touch data/ so the training
 provenance contracts keep passing.
To teach Fresh AI something new, add a row to freshaiknowledge with
projectid = ''fresh-web-lite-platform'' and userid = null, plus one or two
freshaitrainingexamples.','docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md','927026f15dc8bb72'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP — 6. How Fresh AI answers (independent)','Per docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md (Fresh powers and missions map), section "6. How Fresh AI answers (independent)": Verified in code: the gateway uses Fresh''s own kernel. This bundle removes the only outside
AI call in the API layer (Gemini in api/ai/ask.ts), so Fresh AI no longer depends on
Gemini, DeepSeek or any other provider. The kernel''s native answer layer returns templates
when it has no evidence; with evidence it answers from it. ask.ts now retrieves
freshaiknowledge rows on every request and the kernel answers directly from them when
no fresh evidence is needed. See docs/FRESHAIINDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md for the stages
toward a fully self-trained model.','docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md','42b23f5352ca2cd5'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP — 7. Open items not fixed by this bundle','Per docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md (Fresh powers and missions map), section "7. Open items not fixed by this bundle": - users.subscription, users.stats and users.security are still editable by
 the row owner. Lock them once client usage is checked.
- /api/ai/ask accepts anonymous callers. Require auth or add a rate limit.
- About 25 migrations are no-op stubs. Run supabase db pull for a real baseline.
- Leaked-password protection is off (Supabase Auth settings).
- Legacy Vercel integration variables point at another Supabase project. Remove them.
- README is stale (20 ecosystems, "no database").','docs/FRESH_POWERS_MISSIONS_MAP.md','bf9d667e16209fd3'),
