This document covers platform layers through Definition of Done and completion test. Sections 26–40 (Control Plane, Source-of-Truth Registry, Policy Engine, Trust Graph, AI safety boundary, events/state, idempotency, threat modeling, data lifecycle, release/flags, providers, capacity, 18 invariants, implementation ledger, acceptance test) live in the Control/Safety/Operations companion.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md','6f1412fd9318c47a'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE — 8.2 Architecture rule','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md (Fresh Web Lite — Platform Architecture & Governance), section "8.2 Architecture rule": Every ecosystem must use shared platform services where the capability already exists. No competing identity, permission, notification, search, payment, trust, analytics, AI memory, or user/profile system without explicit architectural justification.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md','5979673de0bf5d58'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE — 9–25','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md (Fresh Web Lite — Platform Architecture & Governance), section "9–25": Full text for Canonical Data Model, Fresh ID, TRUEMODE, AI Governance, API/Events, Persistence, Security, DR, Observability, Gates G0–G11, Portability, Versioning, Definition of Done, Implementation Truth, Change Control, Governance Principle, and Completion Test remains as previously locked in this repository history and on Google Drive (34a LOCKED).
Continue to: FRESHWEBLITEPLATFORMCONTROLSAFETYOPERATIONS.md for sections 26–40.
Locked: 2026-09-23. Sections 8–25. See companion for 26–40.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md','ac466de3bddf6fd6'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — Purpose','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "Purpose": Fresh Web Lite shall be designed not merely as another application, social network, search engine, or collection of features.
It shall be designed as a universal digital platform: a trusted layer through which people can discover, communicate, create, learn, work, manage their digital identity, interact with intelligent systems, and move between digital services without losing control of their identity, data, context, or freedom.
The ambition is not to force humanity to use Fresh Web Lite.
The ambition is to make Fresh Web Lite so useful, interoperable, trustworthy, accessible, and deeply integrated into digital life that people naturally choose it.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','c4ac9f4a70c4a084'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 1. THE UNIVERSAL PRINCIPLE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "1. THE UNIVERSAL PRINCIPLE": Fresh Web Lite should follow one fundamental principle:
One platform should connect many aspects of digital life without becoming a prison.
Fresh Web Lite must therefore avoid becoming a closed ecosystem where users are trapped.
A person should be able to enter Fresh Web Lite, use its capabilities, connect with other people and services, create and discover information, and still retain meaningful ownership and control over their digital identity and information.
Universality must come from usefulness and interoperability, not coercion.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','d61fc2bab69565a8'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 2. THE FRESH WEB LITE VISION','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "2. THE FRESH WEB LITE VISION": Fresh Web Lite should evolve toward a digital environment where a person can move naturally between:
- Communication
- Creation
- Discovery
- Learning
- Work
- Digital Life
- Search
- Media
- Communities
- Commerce
- Identity
- AI
- Software
- Future technologies
These should not feel like unrelated applications.
They should operate as interconnected parts of one coherent platform.
The user should not constantly ask:
“Which application do I need for this?”
Instead, Fresh Web Lite should increasingly understand:
“What are you trying to accomplish?”
and help the user reach the appropriate capability.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','8ec24c7fb8823e5f'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 3. FRESH IDENTITY','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "3. FRESH IDENTITY": Fresh Web Lite should establish Fresh ID as a portable digital identity layer.
Fresh ID should become more than a username and profile picture.
It should potentially represent:
- Identity
- Profile
- Skills
- Achievements
- Contributions
- Creative work
- Professional activity
- Communities
- Relationships
- Reputation
- Permissions
- Preferences
- Personal context
However, reputation must never become an unquestionable social ranking.
Users must retain the ability to understand, control, correct, and where appropriate remove information associated with their identity.
Fresh ID should ultimately allow a person to have one coherent digital presence across Fresh Web Lite ecosystems instead of repeatedly rebuilding their identity in every service.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','e5b145ffe90c4dfe'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 4. FRESH FLOW AS THE UNIVERSAL MEDIA LAYER','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "4. FRESH FLOW AS THE UNIVERSAL MEDIA LAYER": Fresh Flow should become the platform''s media and information environment.
It should accommodate different forms of expression rather than reducing everything to one content format:
- Short-form video
- Long-form video
- News and posts
- Podcasts
- Audio
- AR
- VR
- Images
- Text
- Live experiences
- Future media formats
Each medium can have its own appropriate interaction model while maintaining the same Fresh design language.
Fresh Flow should prioritize:
Authentic Engagement Over Virality.
The system should optimize not merely for time spent, but for meaningful discovery, useful information, creativity, relationships, learning, and user satisfaction.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','9e85f52f59af52c2'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 5. FRESH INTELLIGENCE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "5. FRESH INTELLIGENCE": Artificial intelligence should not be an isolated chatbot inside Fresh Web Lite.
It should become an intelligence layer across the platform.
Fresh Intelligence should eventually support:
- Context understanding
- Personalization
- Intelligent search
- Knowledge discovery
- Recommendations
- Translation
- Personal memory
- Goal assistance
- Cross-ecosystem navigation
- Creative assistance
- Research
- Software development
- Workflow automation
- Agent systems
The intelligence layer must operate under a fundamental rule:
AI should increase human capability without quietly taking away human agency.
Important actions should remain understandable and controllable.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','a79b4799fa87e319'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 6. PERSONAL DIGITAL OS','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "6. PERSONAL DIGITAL OS": Fresh Web Lite should progressively become a person''s Personal Digital Operating Environment.
The platform should understand enough context to help users move between activities naturally.
For example:
A person may begin with a message.
That message may lead to research.
Research may lead to a document.
The document may lead to collaboration.
Collaboration may lead to a project.
The project may lead to payment or commerce.
Fresh Web Lite should be capable of connecting these transitions instead of forcing the user to repeatedly restart their digital journey.
The platform should therefore think in terms of:
intent → context → action → outcome
rather than:
application → screen → feature.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','351719d0f914d702'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 7. UNIVERSAL SEARCH','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "7. UNIVERSAL SEARCH": Fresh Web Lite should develop search beyond traditional keyword retrieval.
The long-term objective should be:
Search for information, people, media, knowledge, services, actions, and outcomes from one intelligent environment.
Search should support:
- Text
- Voice
- Visual information
- Translation
- Semantic understanding
- Cross-ecosystem discovery
- Personal context
- Public knowledge
- Fresh Flow content
- Connected services
The user should be able to express what they want naturally rather than learning complicated search syntax.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','8abf1320b904ff07'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 8. UNIVERSAL KNOWLEDGE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "8. UNIVERSAL KNOWLEDGE": Fresh Web Lite should develop a Fresh Knowledge Network capable of connecting information across the platform.
Knowledge should not merely be stored as isolated pages.
The system should understand relationships between:
- People
- Ideas
- Events
- Organizations
- Media
- Skills
- Places
- Projects
- Products
- Documents
- Communities
This can form a living knowledge graph that helps users discover meaningful relationships.
AI should assist in navigating this knowledge while clearly distinguishing:
- verified information
- uncertain information
- generated information
- user-provided information','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','9e2f0d64682c18fa'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 9. UNIVERSAL AGENT SYSTEM','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "9. UNIVERSAL AGENT SYSTEM": Fresh Web Lite may eventually contain specialized AI agents capable of assisting with different tasks.
Examples include:
- Research Agent
- Creation Agent
- Learning Agent
- Work Agent
- Development Agent
- Discovery Agent
- Personal Assistant
- Commerce Assistant
- Knowledge Agent
These agents should operate within explicit permissions.
The principle should be:
Capability must never automatically imply authority.
An agent may be capable of performing an action without being authorized to perform it.
Users must be able to see and control meaningful permissions.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','b649599d3d73f6c1'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 10. AUTONOMOUS ENGINEERING','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "10. AUTONOMOUS ENGINEERING": Fresh Web Lite should eventually contain an Autonomous Engineering Engine.
Its purpose should be to help build Fresh Web Lite itself.
It may:
- Inspect the existing system
- Detect missing implementations
- Identify bugs
- Propose architecture
- Generate code
- Create tests
- Analyze failures
- Recommend improvements
- Prepare changes
But the system should not silently deploy arbitrary changes.
The default principle should be:
Discover → Explain → Propose → Test → Request Approval → Merge → Deploy
This creates a platform capable of improving itself while retaining human governance.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','bb67c71c8cdd1421'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 11. INTEROPERABILITY','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "11. INTEROPERABILITY": A universal platform must not depend entirely on isolation.
Fresh Web Lite should progressively support responsible interoperability with external services and ecosystems.
The objective should be:
Fresh Web Lite should connect the digital world, not pretend the digital world ends at Fresh Web Lite.
Where technically and legally possible, users should be able to:
- Import information
- Export information
- Connect services
- Move their identity
- Transfer appropriate data
- Integrate external tools
- Maintain continuity across platforms
Portability should be treated as a foundational principle rather than a later feature.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','7d91813840bf2074'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 12. USER OWNERSHIP','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "12. USER OWNERSHIP": Fresh Web Lite must establish a strong principle of:
My identity. 
My information. 
My choices. 
My permissions.
Users should have meaningful control over:
- Their profile
- Their content
- Their connections
- Their preferences
- Their data
- Their AI context
- Their permissions
- Their connected services
Fresh Web Lite should not deliberately create unnecessary dependence by making users unable to leave.
Paradoxically, making the platform trustworthy enough to leave can make people more willing to stay.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','91a00cdffc9a9d84'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 13. PRIVACY BY ARCHITECTURE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "13. PRIVACY BY ARCHITECTURE": Privacy should not be treated as a marketing sentence.
It should influence the architecture.
Fresh Web Lite should minimize unnecessary data collection and protect sensitive information through appropriate:
- Authentication
- Authorization
- Encryption
- Access controls
- Isolation
- Auditability
- Data minimization
- Retention policies
- Security monitoring
Users should see useful outcomes without being exposed to internal implementation details, secrets, proprietary logic, or private system architecture.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','60067ab431494261'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 14. TRUST LAYER','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "14. TRUST LAYER": Fresh Web Lite should establish a platform-wide Trust Layer.
Trust should apply to:
- Identity
- Content
- AI outputs
- Recommendations
- Transactions
- Reputation
- Software
- Communities
- External integrations
The system should communicate uncertainty honestly.
Fresh Web Lite must never manufacture certainty merely because certainty looks better in the interface.
A fundamental rule:
True before impressive.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','526eab2c6d1e2889'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 15. HUMAN-CENTERED GOVERNANCE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "15. HUMAN-CENTERED GOVERNANCE": The platform must remain accountable to people.
As Fresh Web Lite becomes more capable, governance must become stronger rather than weaker.
Major systems should have:
- Clear ownership
- Permission boundaries
- Audit trails
- Safety controls
- Human override
- Incident response
- Abuse prevention
- Security review
- Independent testing where appropriate
No AI component should automatically become the final authority simply because it is highly capable.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','7fb1e157d7fd57ac'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 16. ANTI-ADDICTION DESIGN','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "16. ANTI-ADDICTION DESIGN": Fresh Web Lite should reject the assumption that a successful platform must maximize user addiction.
The primary objective should be:
Value created per meaningful interaction.
The platform should encourage:
- Healthy usage
- Authentic relationships
- Useful discovery
- Creativity
- Learning
- Productivity
- Community
- Personal growth
Metrics such as engagement should never become the sole definition of success.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','20f69b8aa22a86e8'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 17. UNIVERSAL ACCESSIBILITY','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "17. UNIVERSAL ACCESSIBILITY": If Fresh Web Lite is intended to become universal, it must be designed for people with different:
- Devices
- Network conditions
- Languages
- Abilities
- Technical skills
- Economic circumstances
- Cultural environments
The experience should progressively support:
low-end devices → modern phones → computers → immersive devices → future interfaces.
The platform must not assume that everyone has the same hardware or connectivity.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','67839f283b9774fb'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 18. ONE DESIGN LANGUAGE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "18. ONE DESIGN LANGUAGE": Fresh Web Lite should maintain a recognizable visual and interaction identity across its ecosystems.
The platform can contain many experiences without becoming visually fragmented.
The principle is:
Many worlds. One Fresh language.
Navigation, typography, motion, icons, interaction patterns, accessibility, feedback, and system states should evolve from a coherent design system.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','794280b18651c437'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 19. ECOSYSTEM ARCHITECTURE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "19. ECOSYSTEM ARCHITECTURE": Fresh Web Lite should be structured so new ecosystems can be added without destroying the foundation.
The core should provide reusable capabilities such as:
- Identity
- Search
- Intelligence
- Permissions
- Notifications
- Payments
- Media
- Storage
- Profiles
- Social graph
- Knowledge
- Developer infrastructure
Individual ecosystems should consume these capabilities instead of rebuilding them independently.
This creates a platform rather than a collection of disconnected applications.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','50504adb1bafc8c3'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 20. ECONOMIC LAYER','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "20. ECONOMIC LAYER": Fresh Web Lite should eventually enable users, creators, developers, businesses, and communities to participate economically.
Potential areas include:
- Creator economy
- Digital services
- Marketplace
- Software ecosystem
- Professional services
- Payments
- Fresh Wallet
- Fresh Currency
- Future digital assets
Economic systems must be designed around transparency, security, lawful operation, and user protection.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','7c1fa0b2c560b84d'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 21. FRESH SOFTWARE ECOSYSTEM','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "21. FRESH SOFTWARE ECOSYSTEM": Fresh Web Lite should eventually become more than an application.
It should provide a platform on which developers can build.
The ecosystem may include:
- APIs
- SDKs
- Developer tools
- AI capabilities
- Identity services
- Data interfaces
- Extensions
- Device-aware applications
- Adaptive interfaces
- Publishing systems
This is how Fresh Web Lite can grow from a product into an ecosystem.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','4450ea561e62c25c'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 22. THE FRESH PRINCIPLE OF SCALE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "22. THE FRESH PRINCIPLE OF SCALE": Fresh Web Lite should be built as though millions or billions of people may eventually depend upon it—but it must earn that scale gradually.
Therefore:
Do not build fake scale. Build scalable foundations.
Every major subsystem should be evaluated for:
- Reliability
- Performance
- Security
- Observability
- Maintainability
- Cost
- Failure recovery
- Data integrity
- Migration capability
A feature that works in a demonstration but cannot survive real users is not considered complete.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','4b0f245598de1b9d'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 23. THE UNIVERSAL PLATFORM TEST','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "23. THE UNIVERSAL PLATFORM TEST": Every major Fresh Web Lite feature should answer five questions:
1. Does it create genuine value?
If removing it makes the user''s life no worse, reconsider it.
2. Does it connect to the larger platform?
Avoid unnecessary isolated features.
3. Does it preserve user agency?
The system should assist rather than quietly dominate decisions.
4. Can it scale responsibly?
Prototype success is not production success.
5. Does it move Fresh Web Lite toward universality?
If not, it may be distraction rather than progress.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','81f9d419f8415f25'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 24. THE FRESH WEB LITE NORTH STAR','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "24. THE FRESH WEB LITE NORTH STAR": The ultimate objective can be expressed simply:
Fresh Web Lite should become a universal digital environment where people can live, connect, create, discover, learn, work, transact, and interact with intelligent technology—while retaining ownership, freedom, privacy, identity, and control.
Not a replacement for humanity.
Not a digital prison.
Not merely another social network.
Not merely an AI chatbot.
Not merely a search engine.
Not merely a media platform.
A connected digital foundation.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','bafdad68d295c202'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 25. THE WATER PRINCIPLE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "25. THE WATER PRINCIPLE": The water analogy should become a philosophical reference for Fresh Web Lite.
Water is valuable because it supports life.
Fresh Web Lite should aim to become valuable because it supports digital life.
But there is an essential difference:
Water is naturally necessary for biological life.
Fresh Web Lite must never claim that people are biologically or politically required to use it.
Therefore:
Universality must be earned, never imposed.
The strongest form of universal adoption is voluntary dependence created by genuine value.
People should choose Fresh Web Lite because it makes their digital lives:
simpler, safer, smarter, more connected, more creative, more productive, and more free.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','f2292a4640a10916'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — 26. THE FINAL PRINCIPLE','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "26. THE FINAL PRINCIPLE": Fresh Web Lite should never measure its success by how much control it has over people.
It should measure success by how much capability it gives people.
The greater Fresh Web Lite becomes, the more important this principle becomes:
Power for the platform must translate into power for the person.
If Fresh Web Lite becomes enormous but users lose control, the mission has failed.
If Fresh Web Lite becomes enormous because it gives people extraordinary capability while preserving their freedom, privacy, identity, and choice, then the original ambition has been fulfilled.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','e88e38e02888fd1e'),
 ('Doc: FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE — FRESH WEB LITE NORTH STAR STATEMENT','Per docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md (FRESH WEB LITE), section "FRESH WEB LITE NORTH STAR STATEMENT": Fresh Web Lite is a universal digital platform designed to connect intelligence, identity, media, communication, creation, knowledge, work, discovery, and digital life into one trusted ecosystem—built to expand human capability while preserving human agency.
One identity. 
One intelligent foundation. 
Many ecosystems. 
Open connections. 
Human control.
Build it true. 
Build it useful. 
Build it universal. 
Build it for humanity.','docs/FRESH_WEB_LITE_UNIVERSAL_PLATFORM_DOCTRINE.md','0c5e08530839b9d9'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Core experience','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Core experience": - Full-screen immersive viewer.
- Up/down navigation for the media stream.
- Left/right navigation for creator, context, related media, evidence and source spaces.
- Keyboard, buttons and accessibility alternatives for every gesture.
- Intent modes: Discover, Learn, Research, News, Relax and Create.
- Quiet mode and anti-infinite-scroll controls.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','16ef4a8d2f14317b'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Comments and replies','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Comments and replies": Every Short can support a unified comment composer with:
- text comments;
- video comments;
- audio/voice comments;
- image comments;
- galleries/multiple images;
- mixed attachments;
- replies and threaded replies;
- mentions and links;
- edit/delete/report/moderation controls;
- creator pinning and reply highlighting.
Comment attachments use the same media pipeline as first-class Fresh media. They are not treated as opaque blobs.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','fe4579e541f31b8d'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Reactions','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Reactions": Support standard reactions plus richer semantic reactions:
- Like, Love, Laugh, Wow, Celebrate, Support;
- Curious, Inspire, Insightful, Agree, Disagree, Helpful, Question, Respect;
- Fire, Sad, Angry;
- future custom reactions defined by Fresh without changing the core interaction model.
Reaction analytics must not force all reactions into a single engagement score. The system should preserve reaction intent.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','0b92628e1fd8f2fa'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Creator Studio','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Creator Studio": - Record or upload.
- Multi-clip editing, trim, split, reorder, crop and speed.
- Text, captions, stickers, effects and filters.
- Voice-over, music and sound mixing.
- Cover selection.
- Drafts/autosave.
- Publish, schedule and visibility controls.
- AI captions, translation, reframing, highlight extraction and long-video-to-Short generation.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','9574b9afb183b98f'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Media relationships','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Media relationships": - Long video -> Shorts.
- Short -> original/full video.
- News -> Short -> full story.
- Live -> highlight -> Short -> replay.
- Post -> related media -> context.
- Remix lineage preserves attribution from original through every remix.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','7545e878612b9c13'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — #TrueMode integration','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "#TrueMode integration": - Why am I seeing this?
- Context Lens.
- Mystery Mode.
- Perspective Mode.
- Reality Check.
- Deep Mode.
- Serendipity.
- Time Lens.
- Memory Echo.
- Origin Trace.
- Contradiction Detector.
- Investigation Mode.
- Personal Discovery Map.
- Intent Feed.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','c10fd47b55224a71'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Trust and safety','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Trust and safety": - Provenance and source information.
- AI-assisted/generated disclosure where applicable.
- Copyright and reporting controls.
- Block, mute and not-interested controls.
- Clear distinction between confirmed, supported, disputed and unknown information.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','54fc9d8780d45926'),
 ('Doc: SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC — Interaction principle','Per docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md (Fresh Shorts — Final Product Specification), section "Interaction principle": Shorts is not a one-dimensional infinite-scroll product. It is a navigable media space where movement, context, creation, conversation and knowledge are connected.','docs/SHORTS_FINAL_SPEC.md','abd9fc1730792383'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Purpose','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Purpose": #TrueMode is the interaction philosophy for Fresh media: help people explore information without hiding the world behind an opaque engagement loop.','docs/TRUEMODE.md','0c564a36b5b116e2'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Core features (part 1/2)','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Core features": - 2D Media Navigation: up/down moves through media; left/right opens context, creator space, related media or evidence.
- Context Lens: source, provenance, timeline and uncertainty.
- Why Am I Seeing This?: transparent recommendation signals and user control over those signals.
- Intent Feed: Discover, Learn, Research, News, Relax and Create.
- Mystery Mode: clue -> context -> connection -> discovery; never fabricate a mystery or fact.
- Perspective Mode: separate official, independent, witness, expert and community perspectives.
- Reality Check: distinguish confirmed, supported, disputed and unknown.
- Deep Mode: Short -> explanation -> full media/article -> notes -> learning path.
- Serendipity Engine: controlled useful distant connections instead of similarity-only recommendations.
- Quiet Feed: reduce pressure, notifications and infinite-scroll mechanics.
- Invisible Mode: browsing that does not permanently change personalization when enabled.
- Forget This: remove an interaction from personalization/memory where supported.','docs/TRUEMODE.md','ffaf08a01f2bbf77'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Core features (part 2/2)','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Core features": - Memory Echo: surface earlier related encounters and compare what changed.
- Time Lens: origin -> development -> turning points -> current state.
- Future Lens: known -> emerging -> speculative, with assumptions separated.
- Origin Trace: preserve original -> edit -> remix lineage.
- Media Current: follow an evolving story rather than isolated posts.
- Investigation Mode: collect media, documents and evidence into a connected workspace.
- Contradiction Detector: surface disagreements instead of silently resolving them.
- Story Weaver: combine posts, Shorts, News, Videos and documents into a source-preserving timeline.
- Question Generator: suggest useful questions the user may not have considered.
- Rabbit-Hole Navigator: choose a deliberate path through a topic.
- Hidden Door: reveal legitimate connections that are not obvious from the current item.
- Unknown Layer: explicitly show what is not established.
- Take Me Somewhere Unexpected: bounded surprise discovery.','docs/TRUEMODE.md','c48fc0da340225a3'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Media relationships','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Media relationships": Shorts, long videos, posts, News, Live, Stories, Photos, Audio and Articles should share a common media identity while retaining type-specific behavior.
Key paths:
- Long Video -> Short -> original video
- News -> Short -> full story
- Live -> highlight -> Short -> replay
- Post -> related media -> context
- Media -> source -> provenance -> discussion','docs/TRUEMODE.md','61a8ede1a1190963'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Phase 1: interaction foundation','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Phase 1: interaction foundation": - TrueMode Hub
- Intent state
- 2D gesture prototype
- Context Lens
- Why This
- Mystery Mode
- Perspective / Reality Check
- Deep Mode / Serendipity controls','docs/TRUEMODE.md','4bb2b76e9d16a10f'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Phase 2: media integration','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Phase 2: media integration": - Connect TrueMode to the unified media model.
- Add gesture routing to Shorts and media viewer.
- Add source/provenance relationships.
- Add creator, topic, article, video and Live context.','docs/TRUEMODE.md','ae93aaf834247c3a'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Phase 3: intelligence','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Phase 3: intelligence": - Personal Discovery Map
- Memory Echo
- Time Lens
- Question Generator
- Contradiction Detector
- Investigation Mode
- Story Weaver','docs/TRUEMODE.md','61f90e0018367143'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Phase 4: user sovereignty','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Phase 4: user sovereignty": - Invisible Mode
- Forget This
- recommendation signal controls
- attention/session controls
- portable provenance and media identity','docs/TRUEMODE.md','72e9f27a75973877'),
 ('Doc: TRUEMODE — Safety and trust rule','Per docs/TRUEMODE.md (Fresh #TrueMode), section "Safety and trust rule": Mystery, discovery and AI explanations must never imply evidence that does not exist. Unknown information remains unknown, and inference must remain distinguishable from source-backed fact.','docs/TRUEMODE.md','7a37e41edca0b6b3')
), upd as (
  update public.fresh_ai_knowledge k
  set content = d.content,
      source = d.source,
      metadata = coalesce(k.metadata, '{}'::jsonb) || jsonb_build_object('dataset', 'platform-docs-v1', 'content_hash', d.hash),
      updated_at = now()
  from d
  where k.project_id = 'fresh-web-lite-platform' and k.user_id is null and k.title = d.title
    and coalesce(k.metadata->>'content_hash', '') <> d.hash
  returning 1
)
insert into public.fresh_ai_knowledge (user_id, project_id, title, content, modality, source, provenance, truth_state, confidence, metadata)
select null, 'fresh-web-lite-platform', d.title, d.content, 'text', d.source,
       jsonb_build_object('kind', 'first-party', 'generator', 'generate-fresh-knowledge-from-docs'),
       'PROBABLE', 0.75, jsonb_build_object('dataset', 'platform-docs-v1', 'content_hash', d.hash)
from d
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.fresh_ai_knowledge k
  where k.project_id = 'fresh-web-lite-platform' and k.user_id is null and k.title = d.title
);

notify pgrst, 'reload schema';
